{
  "id": "posters",
  "content": {
    "description": [
      [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "When Design Photo received a 28-by-49-inch monitor to promote its services, "
            },
            {
              "type": "external-link",
              "href": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jogindersinghphotography/",
              "label": "Joginder Singh"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": " saw it as the foundation for a visual identity we could refine over time. With limited shift time for student monitors, we needed a modular template that any staff member with basic design sensibilities could adapt, distinctive enough to read as Design Photography yet aligned with OCAD University, including Gotham from the 2011 rebrand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "The palette centred on red from "
            },
            {
              "type": "external-link",
              "href": "https://www.ocadu.ca/news/lighten-open-access-wall-studio",
              "label": "Lighten Up! The Open Access Wall Studio"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": ", linking the studio’s earlier work to the new system. Typography, colour, and layout together gave Design Photography a flexible, recognisable voice across notices, events, and information graphics for everyday use."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    ],
